and whether it is scoped to the tickets remote), so the match rule is unambiguous.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["for-each-ref emits full names like refs/remotes/origin/tickets (commit_impact.py:185)","Plan says exclude 'refs/remotes/<remote>/tickets' in AC4 but the prose describes the rule as excluding a branch name, not a fully-qualified per-remote ref","tickets_branch(root) is remote-agnostic; tickets_remote(root) is a separate accessor (config.py:225)"],"finding":"The exclusion rule ('exclude the configured ticket event-log branch') is specified at the branch-name level, but remote-tracking refs are refs/remotes/<remote>/<branch>; the plan does not specify that the match is on the trailing branch component, leaving ambiguous whether it excludes only refs/remotes/<tickets_remote>/<tickets_branch> or any ref ending in that branch name across all remotes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4325a7fb5035b8e8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Determination section, last paragraph ('config.tickets_branch()') / AC line 4","norm_id":"nc1510be26f98ede9","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A repo with multiple remotes, or a code branch on another remote that happens to share the tickets branch name"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable